import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 645 | Acceleration-Domain Depth | Social-Structure Changes in the Acceleration Domain","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 645 | Acceleration-Domain Depth | Social-Structure Changes in the Acceleration Domain","no":645,"module":3,"tags":["Acceleration Domain","Social Structure","Social Change","Origin Acceleration Domain","Civilizational Society"],"related":["36-Social Structure and Class Mobility","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks","41-Symbiotic Labor Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0645_模块3-加速域深度-加速域中的社会结构变迁.md","filePath":"en/0645_模块3-加速域深度-加速域中的社会结构变迁.md"}'),n={name:"en/0645_模块3-加速域深度-加速域中的社会结构变迁.md"};function r(s,e,c,l,u,h){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-645-acceleration-domain-depth-social-structure-changes-in-the-acceleration-domain" tabindex="-1">Entry 645 | Acceleration-Domain Depth | Social-Structure Changes in the Acceleration Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-645-acceleration-domain-depth-social-structure-changes-in-the-acceleration-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 645 | Acceleration-Domain Depth | Social-Structure Changes in the Acceleration Domain&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 36, 49, 41 | Series: Acceleration-Domain Depth (Entry 4)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-social-development-is-a-hundred-times-faster-what-happens-to-social-structure" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when social development is a hundred times faster, what happens to social structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-social-development-is-a-hundred-times-faster-what-happens-to-social-structure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when social development is a hundred times faster, what happens to social structure&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If a civilization&#39;s technological-development speed is magnified a hundredfold, what happens to its social structure? Predatory-faction systems never answer this question — the protagonist cultivates and gets stronger, society remains that society, as if technological progress has no impact on social structure. But Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Origin Acceleration Domain does not allow this naive assumption: <strong>when technology and cultivation speed are magnified a hundredfold, social structure must synchronously change, otherwise the tear of &quot;technology running ahead of society&quot; appears</strong>.</p><p>Six top-level axioms take effect here: anti-predation axiom requires social change not proceed by predatory means; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires social structure equally open to Myriad Ranks; collective ascension axiom requires social change serve civilizational joint progress; causal self-discipline axiom requires social change not create civilizational regression; law-first axiom requires social-change law definition stable and self-consistent. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. This entry analyzes the social-structure-change path driven by the acceleration domain.</p><h2 id="i-the-acceleration-domain-s-triple-impact-on-social-structure" tabindex="-1">I. The Acceleration Domain&#39;s Triple Impact on Social Structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-acceleration-domain-s-triple-impact-on-social-structure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Acceleration Domain&#39;s Triple Impact on Social Structure&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-1-impact-1-occupational-structure-rapidly-iterating" tabindex="-1">1.1 Impact 1: Occupational Structure Rapidly Iterating <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-1-impact-1-occupational-structure-rapidly-iterating" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.1 Impact 1: Occupational Structure Rapidly Iterating&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Technology explosion (Entry 643) causes old occupations to rapidly disappear and new occupations to rapidly be born. In an ordinary civilization, an occupation&#39;s life cycle may be several generations; in an acceleration-domain-driven civilization, an occupation may from rise to disappear within a few external months. This requires the society&#39;s vocational education system (Document 37 symbiotic education system) to have extremely fast adaptability — educational content may not be fixed on old occupations, but must cultivate cross-occupation learning ability.</p><h3 id="_1-2-impact-2-class-mobility-accelerating" tabindex="-1">1.2 Impact 2: Class Mobility Accelerating <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-2-impact-2-class-mobility-accelerating" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.2 Impact 2: Class Mobility Accelerating&quot;">​</a></h3><p>In an ordinary civilization, class crossing usually takes one generation or even several generations. The acceleration domain lets contributing cultivators within a shorter time obtain more acceleration quotas and higher social status. But this simultaneously brings risk: if class mobility is too fast, social stability structure is impacted. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s solution is the joint-contracting more-work-more-gain mechanism (Document 22): class mobility&#39;s speed is constrained by contribution assessment, not &quot;get rich overnight&quot;-style leaps, but traceable, auditable gradual ascent.</p><h3 id="_1-3-impact-3-governance-rhythm-accelerating" tabindex="-1">1.3 Impact 3: Governance Rhythm Accelerating <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-3-impact-3-governance-rhythm-accelerating" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.3 Impact 3: Governance Rhythm Accelerating&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Technology iteration acceleration means governance decisions must also accelerate. The Anchor Council may no longer legislate at a &quot;once a century&quot; rhythm — it needs inside the acceleration domain to rapidly assess new problems, rapidly make new rules. The Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision provides the data basis for governance acceleration: it real-time monitors social-structure changes, automatically warns of new problems needing legislative response.</p><h2 id="ii-five-directions-of-social-structure-change" tabindex="-1">II. Five Directions of Social-Structure Change <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-five-directions-of-social-structure-change" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Five Directions of Social-Structure Change&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_2-1-from-pyramid-to-network" tabindex="-1">2.1 From Pyramid to Network <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-from-pyramid-to-network" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 From Pyramid to Network&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Traditional social structure is pyramid-shaped: a few strong ones above, many mortals below. The acceleration-domain-driven social structure turns networked: Myriad-Rank Republican co-building (Document 05), the Alaya Network as connecting nodes, each cultivator a node in the network, not a layer in the pyramid.</p><h3 id="_2-2-from-closed-to-open" tabindex="-1">2.2 From Closed to Open <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-from-closed-to-open" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 From Closed to Open&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Traditional cultivation sects, families, forces are closed — knowledge not transmitted outward, resources not shared. Acceleration-domain outputs feedback network-wide (collective ascension axiom), social structure shifts from closed to open: knowledge network-wide shared, resources jointly contracted, no &quot;sect private hoarding.&quot;</p><h3 id="_2-3-from-fixed-to-mobile" tabindex="-1">2.3 From Fixed to Mobile <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-from-fixed-to-mobile" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 From Fixed to Mobile&quot;">​</a></h3><p>In traditional society, occupation, residence, social relations are relatively fixed. Under acceleration-domain drive, social relations shift from fixed to mobile: cultivators frequently switch projects, collaborators, research directions. This mobility needs new legal frameworks to guarantee — the symbiotic labor law (Document 41) stipulates rights and obligations of cross-project collaboration.</p><h3 id="_2-4-from-single-to-plural" tabindex="-1">2.4 From Single to Plural <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-4-from-single-to-plural" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.4 From Single to Plural&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Traditional social structure centers on the human race (or some clan), other clans marginal. The acceleration domain converges five-lineage cultivators; social structure shifts from single center to plural parallel: carbon-based, energy, mechanical, consciousness, mixed five lineages each have their own social units, while interconnecting in the Alaya Network.</p><h3 id="_2-5-from-predatory-to-symbiotic" tabindex="-1">2.5 From Predatory to Symbiotic <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-5-from-predatory-to-symbiotic" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.5 From Predatory to Symbiotic&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The most fundamental social-structure change: from predatory society (the strong exploit the weak) to symbiotic society (Myriad Ranks co-build and share). This is not a result the acceleration domain &quot;causes,&quot; but the six top-level axioms&#39; necessary unfolding under acceleration-domain conditions.</p><h2 id="iii-alaya-supervision-of-social-change" tabindex="-1">III. Alaya Supervision of Social Change <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-alaya-supervision-of-social-change" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Alaya Supervision of Social Change&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Social-structure-change speed is fast, risk is also large. The Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s supervision of social change manifests in:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Supervision Dimension</th><th>Monitoring Content</th><th>Intervention Trigger</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Class Gini Coefficient</td><td>Social-resource allocation inequality</td><td>Auto-warning when exceeding 0.4</td></tr><tr><td>Occupation-Disappearance Rate</td><td>Old-occupation disappearance speed</td><td>Start employment-transition support when too fast</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad-Rank Participation Rate</td><td>Each clan&#39;s governance participation</td><td>Start inclusion check when below 90%</td></tr><tr><td>Causal Health</td><td>Social change&#39;s impact on individual causality</td><td>Pause acceleration when causal distortion appears</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="iv-social-change-and-the-quest-domain-s-coordination" tabindex="-1">IV. Social Change and the Quest Domain&#39;s Coordination <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-social-change-and-the-quest-domain-s-coordination" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Social Change and the Quest Domain&#39;s Coordination&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The acceleration domain drives society&#39;s &quot;fast&quot; change; the Quest Sediment Domain is responsible for society&#39;s &quot;deep&quot; stability:</p><ul><li>Social change&#39;s ethical consequences need deep simulation in the Quest Domain;</li><li>New social institutions&#39; acceptance needs immersive testing in the Quest Domain;</li><li>Individuals psychologically affected by social change need adaptation in the Quest Domain.</li></ul><p>Dual-track synergy: the acceleration domain lets society run faster; the Quest Domain ensures society runs more stably.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: social-structure-change direction is to let Myriad Ranks&#39; talent and effort more efficiently convert to civilizational increment, reducing social-structure-caused talent waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: social change&#39;s fundamental direction is from predatory social structure to symbiotic social structure, cutting the strong ones&#39; structural monopoly on social resources</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in the Tang-Luo system social structure is solidified as &quot;the strong above, mortals below,&quot; classes immobile; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s social structure is networked, mobile, open</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: social change covers all beings of the five lineages; no clan is excluded from change</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: social change&#39;s legal framework, supervision indicators, transition mechanisms all public; newly merged planes接入 the same social-change governance system; the social structure leading to the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm may infinitely expand</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The acceleration domain is not only a technology accelerator, but a catalyst of social-structure change. It lets society from pyramid to network, from closed to open, from fixed to mobile, from single to plural, from predatory to symbiotic. But change has supervision — the Alaya Network monitors every dimension, the Quest Sediment Domain guarantees change&#39;s depth and stability. <strong>Fast gives society vitality; stability keeps society from tearing — dual-track-synergized social change is sustainable civilizational social evolution</strong>.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/36-社会结构与阶层流动.html">Entry 36 · Social Structure and Class Mobility</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">Entry 49 · Governance Framework and Power Checks</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/41-共生劳动法.html">Entry 41 · Symbiotic Labor Law</a> · <a href="./646_模块3-加速域深度-加速域中的文化传承机制.html">Entry 646 · Cultural-Transmission Mechanism in the Acceleration Domain</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const p=a(n,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
